%e A401828 At generation 1 the firing cells are (0,-1), (1,-1), (0,1), (1,1): each was ready with the two initial firing cells as neighbors. The initial cells become state 2, so a(1) = 4.
%e A401828 At generation 2 the firing cells are (0,-2), (1,-2), (-1,0), (2,0), (0,2), (1,2), each born with two firing neighbors. The previous four firing cells become state 2, while (0,0) and (1,0) become state 3, so a(2) = 6.
